      "writtenOn": "2026-10-14T21:47:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In [`flash_andes_qspi_xip_init()`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/third_party/zephyrproject/zephyr/drivers/flash/flash_andes_qspi_xip.c;l\u003d583-598;drc\u003d362839e0981d546b6520172a03bedc9072ee4dc8), the XIP flash `SCLK` divider is computed from `\u0026spi0`\u0027s `clock-frequency` (`bus_freq`) and [`p25q16`\u0027s `spi-frequency \u003d \u003c50000000\u003e`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/program/fpmcu/et171/common.dtsi;l\u003d34-42;drc\u003db87a766e8569618e7c61a16800b857ea8d127142):\n\n`sclk_div \u003d (bus_freq / (spi_freq \u003c\u003c 1)) - 1` -\u003e `(200 MHz / 100 MHz) - 1 \u003d 1` (`SCLK \u003d 50 MHz`).\n\nHowever, examine the boot initialization order when jumping (`sysjump`) from a 100 MHz RO image to this 200 MHz RW image:\n1. The 100 MHz RO image\u0027s `flash_andes_qspi_xip_init()` sets `SPI0-\u003eIFTIM.SCLK_DIV` (`0xF0B00040`) to `0` (`100 MHz / (2 * (0 + 1)) \u003d 50 MHz`), which persists across the software jump to RW.\n2. In the 200 MHz RW image, [`soc_pre_init()`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/third_party/zephyrproject/modules/hal/egis_module/soc/egis/et171/soc.c;l\u003d118-216;drc\u003d228e22a804096391c93a37e6dcfb14bb41bbb27d) runs at `PRE_KERNEL_1` priority `0` and switches `AOSMU-\u003eCLK_SRC` (`SMU_CLK_AHB`) to 200 MHz (`AHB_CLK_DIV_1`) while `SPI0-\u003eIFTIM.SCLK_DIV` is still `0`.\n3. [`flash_andes_qspi_xip_init()`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/third_party/zephyrproject/zephyr/drivers/flash/flash_andes_qspi_xip.c;l\u003d604-606;drc\u003d362839e0981d546b6520172a03bedc9072ee4dc8) does not run until `POST_KERNEL` priority `50` (`CONFIG_FLASH_INIT_PRIORITY`).\n\nBetween `PRE_KERNEL_1` priority `0` and `POST_KERNEL` priority `50`, XIP instruction fetches from `spi0` will clock the flash at `200 MHz / (2 * (0 + 1)) \u003d 100 MHz` (2x the configured 50 MHz limit).\n\nShould `SPI0-\u003eIFTIM.SCLK_DIV` be updated to `1` before `soc_pre_init()` switches `AOSMU-\u003eCLK_SRC` to 200 MHz (so flash `SCLK` steps from 50 MHz -\u003e 25 MHz -\u003e 50 MHz without exceeding 50 MHz)?",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "bf9b1fff89e68487553a1dca6cb3dc9fb04df42e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
