      "writtenOn": "2026-10-15T08:16:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m aware of that. It\u0027s not a trivial problem. The same happens after cold reboot, when the `SCLK_DIV` has reset value and the clock freq is increased `PRE_KERNEL_1`. I\u0027m not 100% sure how to deal with that. There will always be a window (window between setting system clock freq and SCLK_DIV), when SPI clock speed doesn\u0027t match expected value. There will be similar case when sysjumping to RO, SPI runs at 25MHz for a moment.\n\nIn current case, SPI runs at 100MHz for a moment, which is allowed for the used SPI chip. I would like to hear opinion from @jacky.lee@egistec.corp-partner.google.com and @jason.huang@egistec.corp-partner.google.com how to approach this. \n\nPlease keep in mind that modifying register of SPI used for memory-mapped read is not an easy task. It requires jumping to RAM and handling prefetching and IRQs.",
      "parentUuid": "300e8293_08f27b78",
      "revId": "bf9b1fff89e68487553a1dca6cb3dc9fb04df42e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "797f15b5_68d3da36",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/fpmcu/et171/soc.dtsi",
