      },
      "lineNbr": 71,
      "author": {
        "id": 3698372
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-16T06:13:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Cold boot directly targets the boot ROM via the reset vector, so the flash is not utilized until the SPI clock is configured.\nAlso, as far as I know, a warm boot sets the SPI divider to 1.\nTherefore, even if the AHB is running at 200MHz at that moment, the SPI will still remain at 50MHz.",
      "parentUuid": "dcccabb6_779f80ee",
      "revId": "bf9b1fff89e68487553a1dca6cb3dc9fb04df42e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6a3ce62f_3d2a728a",
