      "writtenOn": "2026-10-14T21:47:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nit: Unlike `spi0` ([`flash_andes_qspi_xip.c`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/third_party/zephyrproject/zephyr/drivers/flash/flash_andes_qspi_xip.c;l\u003d819;drc\u003d362839e0981d546b6520172a03bedc9072ee4dc8), which only reads `clock-frequency`), `spi1` uses [`spi_egis_et171.c`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/third_party/zephyrproject/zephyr/drivers/spi/spi_egis_et171.c;l\u003d1069-1083;drc\u003d5749eb1da43602feff2379164104a0304341fa70), which supports querying `clock_control_get_rate()` when `clock-frequency` is omitted.\n\nConsider configuring `\u0026spi1` similarly to [`\u0026uart0` below](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/program/fpmcu/et171/soc.dtsi;l\u003d83-87;drc\u003d8bb4652603c4cc4a06890100ce98226146060089):\n```dts\n\u0026spi1 {\n\tstatus \u003d \"okay\";\n\t/delete-property/ clock-frequency;\n\tclocks \u003d \u003c\u0026clock ET171_CLOCK_SPIM2\u003e;\n};\n```\nThat way `\u0026spi1` automatically gets the OTP-trimmed `SMU_CLK_AHB` rate from [`et171_clock_control_get_rate()`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/third_party/zephyrproject/modules/hal/egis_module/drivers/clock_control/clock_control_et171.c;l\u003d111-126;drc\u003d73822255050d10a27ef43a8250da97bcba26f9f3) instead of needing a hardcoded frequency kept in sync with `ahb-divide`.",
