      "message": "Since the ET171 APB clock is derived from the AHB clock (`APB_CLOCK \u003d (AHB_CLOCK / 2) / apb_divide` in [`soc_pre_init()`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/third_party/zephyrproject/modules/hal/egis_module/soc/egis/et171/soc.c;l\u003d124-144;drc\u003d228e22a804096391c93a37e6dcfb14bb41bbb27d)), keeping `apb-divide \u003d \u003c1\u003e` while changing `ahb-divide` from `\u003c2\u003e` to `\u003c1\u003e` also doubles `SMU_CLK_APB` from **50 MHz to 100 MHz**.\n\nWhile [`mtimer`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/third_party/zephyrproject/modules/hal/egis_module/soc/egis/et171/soc.c;l\u003d175-178;drc\u003d228e22a804096391c93a37e6dcfb14bb41bbb27d) (and [`power.c`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/third_party/zephyrproject/modules/hal/egis_module/soc/egis/et171/power.c;l\u003d58;drc\u003da9fdf60e64bd0045d5a1c5198dfbe8cc2ce045d6)) and [`uart0`](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/third_party/zephyrproject/modules/hal/egis_module/dts/riscv/egis/clock.dtsi;l\u003d13-15;drc\u003d73822255050d10a27ef43a8250da97bcba26f9f3) query `HAL_SMU_GetClock(SMU_CLK_APB)` at runtime, is 100 MHz within the ET171 hardware specification for the APB bus and all APB peripherals (`uart0`, `gpio0`, `wdt`, `otpc`, `pit0`, `i2c`), or should `apb-divide` be set to `\u003c2\u003e` to keep APB at 50 MHz?",
      "isAi": true,
